---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APP, ROTAS } from '../../i18n';
---

<Base lingua="en" pagina="suporte" titulo="Support" descricao="Support and frequently asked questions for Selah: Enigmas da Bíblia.">
  <article class="documento">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="data">{APP.nome}</p>

    <div class="resumo">
      <p>Found a problem, a content error, or have a suggestion? Write to <a href={`mailto:${APP.email}?subject=Selah%20-%20Support`}><strong>{APP.email}</strong></a>. We reply within 5 business days, in Portuguese or English.</p>
      <p>To help us, include your device model, system version (iOS or Android) and, if relevant, the theme, level and puzzle type.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>Is Selah free?</summary>
      <p>Yes. It has no in-app purchases, subscriptions or ads.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What language is the app in?</summary>
      <p>Brazilian Portuguese.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an account?</summary>
      <p>No. There is no sign-up, email or password. For the leaderboard, the app creates an anonymous account by itself the first time it opens with an internet connection. You only choose a nickname and a character.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an internet connection?</summary>
      <p>No. Once installed, the game works offline. With a connection, the app automatically downloads game fixes and improvements.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I changed phones. How do I bring my progress?</summary>
      <p>Progress is stored only on your device, with no cloud backup, so it does not move to another phone. On the new one, the game starts from the beginning, with a new leaderboard account.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can other players see my nickname?</summary>
      <p>Only if you want them to. The "Show my nickname on the leaderboard" option starts off, so you appear as "Anonymous player". You can change it in the Profile (tap your avatar at the top of the home screen). There is no chat or any other contact between players.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do the leagues work?</summary>
      <p>When you score your first point of the week, you join a group of up to 30 players in your league, from Shepherd to King. The week closes on Sunday at midnight (Brasília time): the top players move up a league, the bottom ones move down, and the best placed win medals, titles, frames and extra hints. On the trail, only improving your stars on a level earns points.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I saw an offensive nickname. How do I report it?</summary>
      <p>On the leaderboard, touch and hold the nickname and choose "Report nickname". The team reviews it and may replace the nickname or block the player.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I erase my progress?</summary>
      <p>In the app, go to Settings › Erase progress. To delete your leaderboard account, open the Profile and tap Delete account. See every step at <a href={ROTAS.excluir.en}>Delete account and data</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I turn the daily reminder on or off?</summary>
      <p>In the app's Settings. Selah sends at most one reminder per day, and only if you turn it on. You can also turn off Selah's notifications in your phone settings.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Sound or music does not play.</summary>
      <p>Check your device volume and the sound and music controls in Settings. On iPhone, the game plays even with the silent switch on; if it still doesn't play, fully close the app and open it again.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I found an error in a clue or verse.</summary>
      <p>Thank you! Write to {APP.email} with the theme, level and text. Verses come from the Bíblia Livre and clues are reviewed with every update.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What age is Selah for?</summary>
      <p>Ages 13 and over. Puzzles have difficulty levels, and the game adapts to each player's pace.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>More information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={ROTAS.privacidade.en}>Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href={ROTAS.termos.en}>Terms of Use</a></li>
      <li><a href={ROTAS.excluir.en}>Delete data</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Developer: {APP.responsavel} · {APP.cidade.en}</p>
  </article>
</Base>
